o pre-v5 rows in the stratified sample don't collapse to 0.0 and corrupt the priority distribution-shift.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tier0.py:92-106 impact_fn_for_row docstring: replaying an old row through the current formula 'silently changes what is being checked' — the shipped decide.impact_plan 'scores such a row's pre-v5 ordinal grades as 0.0'","legacy_v4_baseline.py confirms plan-v4 used ordinal grade vocabulary that decide.impact_plan (plan-v5 closed KIND sets) does not recognize","sampling.py stratum_key includes impact_model_version, so pre-v5 rows are an intended part of the sample","validity axis (decide.validity, pure binary grading) and the impact categorical axis (raw closed-vocab answers) are era-independent; only priority routes through impact_plan"],"finding":"The distribution-shift `priority` axis scores STORED severity attributes through the current fixed `decide.impact_plan`, but the sample deliberately includes pre-v5 rows (it stratifies on `impact_model_version`); a pre-v5 stored row's ordinal grades collapse to 0.0 under the v5 closed-KIND-set formula, so the priority-shift measures an era artifact rather than the prompt-change signal — the exact collapse Tier-0 built `legacy_v4_baseline`/`impact_fn_for_row` to avoid.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9cfcabf071c332ff","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py — distribution_shift() (impact_fn=decide.impact_plan default, line ~334) and the priority computation (s_val * impact_fn(s_attrs), line ~358); plan section 'Distribution shift'","norm_id":"n9a5fa3adb800d868","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A sampled review whose stored decision predates plan-v5 (absent or older impact_model_version): its stored priority collapses toward 0.0 while the candidate's fresh v5-vocabulary answers score normally, inflating the priority total-variation-distance and count deltas with a spurious shift attributed to the prompt change."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In distribution_shift/replay, thread the row's `impact_model_version` (already carried on the sampling-pool row and in sidecar_data) and select `tier0.impact_fn_for_row(data)` for the STORED-side priority computation, mirroring Tier-0; or restrict the priority axis to same-era rows and report the excluded count.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Note the existing `labels.per_question_agreement` in the plan and justify why `tier1.per_question_agreement` is a distinct function (candidate-vs-stored, positional alignment, per-question kappa + no-answer) rather than extending/renaming to avoid the name collision.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["labels.py:214 `def per_question_agreement(review_k, review_k1)` returns `{agreement, comparisons}` by flattening verification answers and matching findings on `norm_id` across two STORED reviews (reviewer-noise measurement)","tier1.py:195 `def per_question_agreement(replayed)` compares a REPLAYED candidate's answers vs stored answers, aligned POSITIONALLY (`zip(..., strict=True)`), split into binary vs severity_attributes with Cohen's kappa + per-question no_answer counts","The plan text nowhere mentions the pre-existing same-named labels helper; a maintainer grepping `per_question_agreement` gets two hits with divergent contracts"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new function tier1.per_question_agreement that shares its exact name and a broadly similar purpose (agreement over per-finding verification answers) with the existing labels.per_question_agreement, without acknowledging the collision or justifying why both coexist.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f928e26458abccd60","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope (src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py per_question_agreement); existing src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py:214","norm_id":"nc50b48992d03b35b","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future reader/maintainer greps per_question_agreement, finds two functions with the same name and different alignment semantics, and cannot tell which is canonical or whether one is dead/duplicate","A later change tries to 'fix' one and misses the other"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the Approach section acknowledging `labels.per_question_agreement` exists for k-vs-k+1 reviewer-noise (norm_id join) and stating that Tier-1's agreement is a distinct candidate-vs-stored, positionally-aligned measurement (hence kappa + no-answer axes), or rename the tier1 function (e.g. `candidate_answer_agreement`) to remove the collision.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["prerequisite-consistency"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Subject: 'the fixed PER_SAMPLE_ESTIMATE_USD[\"tier1\"] = 0.5 pre-flight estimate ($30 for N=60)'","Prerequisite: 'PER_SAMPLE_ESTIMATE_USD = {\"tier1\": 0.5, \"tier2\": 3.4}'","Prerequisite: 'cap_usd and reserve_usd are constants in the module (200 / 30)'","Subject: 'stays well inside the $170 available budget'"],"finding":"The subject plan asserts the pre-flight estimate constant is PER_SAMPLE_ESTIMATE_USD[\"tier1\"] = 0.5, but the ledger prerequisite defines PER_SAMPLE_ESTIMATE_USD = {\"tier1\": 0.5, \"tier2\": 3.4}. The value 0.5 for tier1 is consistent. However, the subject plan states the reserve is $30 (\"$30 for N=60\" for the pre-flight estimate at $0.5/sample) and \"$170 available budget\", implying cap $200 minus reserve $30. The prerequisite fixes LEDGER_RESERVE_USD = 30 and cap = 200, so available = 170. This is consistent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3fe2c7e3d0e64a28","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n7443b06d8146f149","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"fd63f1c170b8aad7","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["488683e36344ba2d",5825],"description_boxes":["eaf16bc07968e013",5],"file_impact":["ccab0092f601c905",8],"ticket_id":["afc5208ac2bc7f37",19]}